    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258-a3">

                <pb facs="0507" n="459" xml:id="pg459"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 120.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moran to Mr.
                            Corvo.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 16,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your excellency’s note of the 10th instant, in reply to the one which I
                    addressed to you on the 19th of December last, under instructions from Mr. Fish,
                    suggesting that His Most Faithful Majesty’s government might be pleased to
                    co-operate with the Governments of the United States and Brazil in the
                    determination telegraphically from Paris of the longitudes of both coasts of
                    South America, and I am gratified to learn that His Majesty’s government is
                    disposed to accede to this request, and that the necessary orders have been and
                    shall be given to that end. I shall at once inform Mr. Fish of this reply, and
                    promptly communicate to your excellency any further information I may receive
                    from my government on the subject.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion to renew to your excellency the assurances of my
                    highest consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>BENJAMIN MORAN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">João de Andrade
                            Corvo</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
